Chrono-Meteorism

Creative Catalyst: Instruments forged from interstellar shrapnel and centuries-old clockwork mechanisms that translate gravity into melody.

Chrono-Meteorism is a sonic excavation of time-space, sounding like a cathedral made of glass collapsing in slow motion. It is defined by the "metallic breath" of meteorite resonators vibrating against escapement gears, creating a timbre that feels simultaneously ancient and hyper-futuristic. The Spitfire Labs ambient guitars are fed through literal clockwork oscillators, resulting in swells that expand and contract like a living lung. It is the sound of a universe winding down its mainspring.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 124–136 BPM, featuring a "gated-swing" rhythm that oscillates between rigid precision and loose, fluid micro-timing.
*   Harmonic Palette: Uses microtonal just-intonation scales, relying on augmented fifths and sub-octave bell-tone clusters to simulate gravity distortion.
   Production Signatures: 1. Ticking-Gating: Side-chaining the low-end to the mechanical release of real gear mechanisms; 2. Magnetic Scrying: Recording onto ferric tape pulled across the raw edges of meteorites; 3. Spatial Stretching*: Using temporal pitch-shifting that preserves the overtone content of ambient guitars while altering the "age" of the wave.
*   Dynamics: A slow, tectonic ascent; tracks begin as quiet rhythmic ticks and bloom into overwhelming, crystalline walls of sound that feel like a solar eclipse.

Scene & Origin Lore
The movement germinated in the "Oubliette Observatory," a deep-crust research station in the Ural Mountains. Its founders, a guild of nomadic horologists turned trans-dimensional lutenists, perform in suits lined with heavy, brass-plated lead to withstand the high-frequency magnetism of their gear. Their rituals involve "Synchrony Seances," where dancers attempt to match the erratic BPM shifts generated by the meteorites, clad in kinetic fashion that ticks and whirs in time with the percussion. It is a clandestine subculture where silence is a commodity and rhythm is a form of weight calculation.

Instruments: Custom-built meteor-guitars (Spitfire Labs samples triggered via magnetic brass coils), escapement-synth oscillators, hydraulic bass-drum modules.

For Fans Of: Rival Consoles, Floating Points, Jon Hopkins, Biosphere.

